  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "The glue block on the smallest trisum glue",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "On the smallest trisum glue (TRISUM-READ's seed 3: 8 lines, 8 points, cycle rank 9), the signed glue's creation map, which by SWITCH-PROOF-20261108-001A is the block of glue lines of every plain edge-atom space with that signing, takes 448 values on the 512 switching classes. It is equivariant under the glue's 24 automorphisms, and of their 42 orbits on the classes it separates all but one pair of orbits of six classes each, those of the signings {(4,4),(5,4),(6,6),(6,7),(7,3)} and {(4,5),(5,4),(6,6),(6,7),(7,3)}, which differ by moving one sign along line 4: their signed glues have 40 and 34 solutions, no automorphism of the incidence graph (those exchanging lines and points included) takes one to the other, and their plain spaces have identical glue blocks. The Pfaffian class is the only class without solutions, and no other class has its block. Each row depends only on the signing's class on the glue without its line, and takes 55 or 57 values on that glue's 128 classes.",
